{"absent":["Enabled KVM paravirt behavior when availability is true, including feature negotiation and async fault token handling.","Layout and lifecycle of hv_clock_per_cpu and pvclock time structures.","Concrete values of PIT_TICK_RATE and configuration symbols for function alignment and padding.","Storage and cross CPU ordering of cmos_lock and implementations of rtc_cmos_read and rtc_cmos_write.","Layouts of struct mce, struct pt_regs, struct cpuinfo_x86 and struct cper_ia_proc_ctx.","Definitions of generic symbol, CFI, ENDBR, stringify and assembly helper macros referenced by linkage helpers.","Semantics and ordering of raw port input output primitives and speaker gate interactions.","Full machine check detection, logging and recovery flow beyond constants and fallback stubs."],"dossier":"D10","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_para.h::kvm_async_pf_task_wait_schedule","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_para.h::kvm_para_available","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_para.h::kvm_arch_para_features","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_para.h::kvm_arch_para_hints","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_para.h::kvm_read_and_reset_apf_flags","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_para.h::kvm_handle_async_pf.alt_2"],"text":"When the routed configuration applies the KVM paravirt helpers present a uniformly disabled interface. Availability probing reports unavailable, feature and hint queries yield zero, flag collection yields zero, async fault handling declines, and task wait scheduling has no effect."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_types.h::KVM_SUB_MODULES.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_types.h::KVM_SUB_MODULES.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_types.h::KVM_SUB_MODULES.alt_3","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_types.h::KVM_ARCH_NR_OBJS_PER_MEMORY_CACHE"],"text":"The build selects KVM submodules as both AMD and Intel together, AMD only, or Intel only across three alternatives. The architecture memory cache size is 40 objects per cache."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_types.h::EXPORT_SYMBOL_FOR_KVM","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_types.h::_ASM_X86_KVM_TYPES_H","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_vcpu_regs.h::_ASM_X86_KVM_VCPU_REGS_H","arch/x86/include/asm/kvmclock.h::_ASM_X86_KVM_CLOCK_H","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::_ASM_X86_LINKAGE_H","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::_ASM_X86_LOCAL_H","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_timer.h::_ASM_X86_MACH_DEFAULT_MACH_TIMER_H","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_traps.h::_ASM_X86_MACH_DEFAULT_MACH_TRAPS_H","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::_ASM_X86_MC146818RTC_H","arch/x86/include/asm/math_emu.h::_ASM_X86_MATH_EMU_H","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::_ASM_X86_MCE_H"],"text":"Routed headers employ include once guards and the KVM symbol export helper expands to nothing here, so annotated symbols receive no additional export treatment in this configuration."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_vcpu_regs.h::__VCPU_REGS_RAX","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_vcpu_regs.h::__VCPU_REGS_RCX","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_vcpu_regs.h::__VCPU_REGS_RDX","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_vcpu_regs.h::__VCPU_REGS_RBX","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_vcpu_regs.h::__VCPU_REGS_RSP","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_vcpu_regs.h::__VCPU_REGS_RBP","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_vcpu_regs.h::__VCPU_REGS_RSI","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_vcpu_regs.h::__VCPU_REGS_RDI","arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_vcpu_regs.h::REG_NUM_INVALID"],"text":"Virtual CPU general register indices run zero through seven in order RAX RCX RDX RBX RSP RBP RSI RDI. The invalid register sentinel is 100."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/kvmclock.h::this_cpu_pvti","arch/x86/include/asm/kvmclock.h::this_cpu_hvclock"],"text":"Per CPU paravirt clock helpers return pointers to the calling CPU clock structures, with the VCPU time pointer obtained from within the hypervisor clock structure of the same CPU."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::notrace","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::_THIS_IP_","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::asmlinkage"],"text":"Function annotations provide a no instrumentation marker, a current address query using RIP relative addressing, and an assembly linkage marker requesting zero register parameters."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::__ALIGN","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::__ALIGN_STR","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::FUNCTION_PADDING.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::FUNCTION_PADDING.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::__FUNC_ALIGN.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::__FUNC_ALIGN.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::ASM_FUNC_ALIGN","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_F_ALIGN"],"text":"Function alignment uses the configured alignment filled with byte 0x90. One build variant adds extra padding after alignment while the other omits it, with stringified equivalents for assembly and symbol use."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::RET.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::RET.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::RET.alt_3","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::ASM_RET.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::ASM_RET.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::ASM_RET.alt_3"],"text":"Return emission offers three build choices covering a jump to a return thunk, a return followed by int3, and a plain return, with matching textual forms for inline assembly."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::CFI_PRE_PADDING.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::CFI_POST_PADDING.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::CFI_PRE_PADDING.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::CFI_POST_PADDING.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::__CFI_TYPE"],"text":"Indirect call type symbols are local function objects embedding byte 0xB8 plus a type identifier stored as a long, with 0x90 fill of configured length placed before the payload in one variant and after it in the other."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_TYPED_FUNC_START","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_FUNC_START","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_FUNC_START_NOALIGN","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_FUNC_START_LOCAL","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_FUNC_START_LOCAL_NOALIGN","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_FUNC_START_WEAK","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_FUNC_START_WEAK_NOALIGN","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_FUNC_ALIAS_MEMFUNC.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_FUNC_ALIAS_MEMFUNC.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_PIC_ALIAS.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/linkage.h::SYM_PIC_ALIAS.alt_2"],"text":"Symbol start helpers cover global local and weak bindings each with aligned and unaligned forms, plus a typed global form that includes ENDBR. Memory function aliasing selects weak or strong form by build and position independent aliasing connects a prefixed name with its canonical target."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::anon_1","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_t","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::LOCAL_INIT","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_read","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_set"],"text":"The local counter wraps a single atomic long. Initialization fixes the starting value while read and set helpers expose the current value and replacement."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_inc","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_dec","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_add","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_sub"],"text":"Basic local updates offer increment decrement and signed add and subtract without returning a status."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_sub_and_test","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_dec_and_test","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_inc_and_test","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_add_negative"],"text":"Conditional local updates indicate whether subtract decrement or increment reached zero and whether an addition yielded a negative outcome."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_add_return","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_sub_return","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_inc_return","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_dec_return","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_cmpxchg","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_try_cmpxchg"],"text":"Value returning local updates deliver the post update result for add subtract increment and decrement. Compare exchange helpers either return the prior value while installing the new one or report boolean success for the conditional attempt."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_xchg","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_add_unless","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::local_inc_not_zero"],"text":"Exchange always installs the requested value and reports the predecessor, retrying until the underlying conditional update succeeds. Conditional add refuses when the observed value matches a forbidden value, otherwise installing the sum, with the not zero increment expressed as unit addition guarding zero."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::__local_inc","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::__local_dec","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::__local_add","arch/x86/include/asm/local.h::__local_sub"],"text":"Double underscore local helpers are direct equivalents of the plain increment decrement add and subtract operations."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mach_timer.h::CALIBRATE_TIME_MSEC","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_timer.h::CALIBRATE_LATCH"],"text":"Calibration timing uses a 30 millisecond interval with a latch value scaled from the platform tick rate to that interval with rounding."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mach_timer.h::mach_prepare_counter","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_timer.h::mach_countup"],"text":"Calibration uses port 0x61 for gate and status, port 0x43 for control and port 0x42 for count transfer, recognizing completion through bit 0x20 of the status port."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mach_timer.h::mach_prepare_counter","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_timer.h::mach_countup"],"text":"Timer calibration entry points prepare the interval channel for mode 0 binary countdown with the derived latch and then measure completion by counting iterations until hardware signaling, delivering the total through a caller location."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mach_traps.h::NMI_REASON_PORT","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_traps.h::NMI_REASON_SERR","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_traps.h::NMI_REASON_IOCHK","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_traps.h::NMI_REASON_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_traps.h::NMI_REASON_CLEAR_SERR","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_traps.h::NMI_REASON_CLEAR_IOCHK","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_traps.h::NMI_REASON_CLEAR_MASK"],"text":"Non maskable interrupt reason decoding uses port 0x61 with bit 0x80 for system error and bit 0x40 for IO check combined into mask 0xC0, with clear controls 0x04 and 0x08 combined into mask 0x0F."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mach_traps.h::reassert_nmi"],"text":"The reassertion path uses CMOS ports 0x70 and 0x71 with selector values 0x8F and 0x0F separated by dummy reads."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mach_traps.h::default_get_nmi_reason","arch/x86/include/asm/mach_traps.h::reassert_nmi"],"text":"Reason reading returns the present status port contents. Reassertion preserves any held CMOS ownership across a toggle through the CMOS ports and then restores the prior lock condition."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::lock_cmos.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::unlock_cmos.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::do_i_have_lock_cmos.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::current_lock_cmos_reg.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::lock_cmos_prefix.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::lock_cmos_suffix.alt_1"],"text":"Enabled CMOS locking stores owning CPU identity plus register in a shared word acquired by repeated compare exchange with relaxation under contention and cleared on release. Ownership and register queries decode the same word and the prefixed section also suppresses local interrupts across the hold."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::lock_cmos.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::unlock_cmos.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::do_i_have_lock_cmos.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::current_lock_cmos_reg.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::lock_cmos_prefix.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::lock_cmos_suffix.alt_2"],"text":"Disabled CMOS locking performs no acquisition or release, always reports absent ownership and zero register, with empty prefix and suffix wrappers that retain no interrupt state."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/math_emu.h::math_emu_info"],"text":"Math emulation information pairs the original instruction pointer value with a pointer to the saved register state."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::RTC_PORT","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::RTC_ALWAYS_BCD","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::CMOS_READ","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::CMOS_WRITE","arch/x86/include/asm/mc146818rtc.h::RTC_IRQ"],"text":"Real time clock addressing adds the register index to base 0x70, binary coded decimal operation is indicated by one, the interrupt line is 8, and byte access is routed through dedicated CMOS read and write helpers."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_BANKCNT_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_CTL_P","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_EXT_P","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_CMCI_P","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_SEAM_NR","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_EXT_CNT_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_EXT_CNT_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_EXT_CNT","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_SER_P","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_ELOG_P","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_LMCE_P"],"text":"Global capability reporting masks bank count with 0xFF and signals features at bit positions 8 9 10 12 24 26 and 27 for control presence extended registers CMCI SEAM recovery extended logging and local check, with an extended count field in bits 16 to 23 extracted by shift 16."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_STATUS_RIPV","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_STATUS_EIPV","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_STATUS_MCIP","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_STATUS_LMCES","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_STATUS_SEAM_NR","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCG_EXT_CTL_LMCE_EN"],"text":"Global status uses bits 0 1 2 3 and 12 for restart address valid correct instruction machine check in progress local signal and SEAM non root, with local enable at bit 0 of the extended control word."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_VAL","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_OVER","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_UC","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_EN","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_MISCV","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_ADDRV","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_PCC","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_S","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_AR","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_CEC_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_CEC_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_CEC","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_MSCOD"],"text":"Bank status high bits 63 through 55 encode valid overflow uncorrected enabled misc valid address valid context corrupt signaled and action required. The corrected count spans bits 38 to 52 extracted by shift 38 and the model specific code comes from bits 16 to 31."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_TCC","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_PADDRV","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_SYNDV","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_DEFERRED","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_POISON","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_STATUS_SCRUB"],"text":"Further status meanings reuse bit 55 for task context corrupt with bits 54 53 44 43 and 40 for physical address valid syndrome valid deferred poison and scrub detection."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_CONFIG_MCAX","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_CONFIG_FRUTEXT","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_CONFIG_PADDRV","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_IPID_MCATYPE","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_IPID_HWID","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCACOD","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCACOD_SCRUB","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCACOD_SCRUBMSK","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCACOD_L3WB","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCACOD_DATA","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCACOD_INSTR"],"text":"Bank configuration uses value 1 with feature bits 9 and 11, identification masks 0xFFFF0000 and 0xFFF, error code mask 0xEFFF with scrub base 0xC0 under mask 0xEFF0 and distinct codes 0x017A 0x0134 and 0x0150 for L3 writeback data load and instruction fetch."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_MISC_ADDR_LSB","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_MISC_ADDR_MODE","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_MISC_ADDR_SEGOFF","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_MISC_ADDR_LINEAR","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_MISC_ADDR_PHYS","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_MISC_ADDR_MEM","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_MISC_ADDR_GENERIC","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_ADDR_PHYSADDR"],"text":"Miscellaneous address decoding takes low 6 bits as bit position and next 3 bits as mode selecting segment offset linear physical memory or generic with values 0 1 2 3 and 7. The physical address mask covers implemented physical bits from zero upward."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_CTL2_CMCI_EN","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCI_CTL2_CMCI_THRESHOLD_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCJ_CTX_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCJ_CTX","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCJ_CTX_RANDOM","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCJ_CTX_PROCESS","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCJ_CTX_IRQ","arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::MCJ_NMI